Z||000026||BlackStang95||10-18-2001||03:38 PM||||I think you've screwed up man, I really do.  I hate the police as much as anyone but you really can't fight them.  I wouldn't put it past an officer to pull you or your son over one night and smack him around a bit with the old nightstick before driving off.  No witnesses, no evidence...what are you gonna do?  If you think cops harass you now just be glad you aren't black...talk about something wrong with our country.||||reg||11
Z||000027||falconhulk||10-18-2001||03:56 PM||||"Here's a free clue, falconhulk - keep the dollar: That which you rail so flailingly against keeps *you* safe. "<P>I am not so hard line as you think man.  I dont think people who break the law should be able to drive.  I agree laws are intended to protect people.  I got no problem with that.  All I am saying is the wording of that statement irratates me.  By the way on that road the only thing that keeps me safe is me.  I am the one that avoids 5 to 6 accidents a day in this hell traffic.  How can you say that the current laws protect you?  You must see the people that want to destroy your propert becasue they have to make a call or feel that 1 space in traffic is worth all of your hard work.  I am as careful as possible when i drive so i hurt no one.  I actually care about other people.  And I dont like being treated like a kid by the same people who drive like kids.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000028||Fiero5||10-18-2001||06:30 PM||||Wow, so many opinions. I love it!<P>Let me respond back to some of these, as some of the statements are a bit incorrect. <P>"mbramble wote:<BR>Seems to me that you don't really want to know what 'everyone' thinks, just those who agree with you. The rest of us are "sheep" who are "partly why the world is the way it is today". You have a mighty high opinion of your opinion."<P>Not true, and I opologize if my comments came off that way.  My sheep comment was meant only at those who said I should have just done whatever I was told. <P>"LZeitgeist wrote:<BR>Hmmmmm... let's see...<P>You didn't want the plates on the front of your cars, so you ignored repeated warnings from officers of the law (and prompted your kid(s) to ignore the warnings, too)"<P>Where did I ever say any of this? This is where things get out of hand when people just pull stuff like this out of the air. My son "chose" to do the same as we did. He could have looked into getting his own plate for his own car, though they are hard to find. It was HIS choice. He is old enough to have a license and the responsibility to drive. He did listen to why myself and his Grandfather did not have our plates on the front, and decided to do the same. As far as the warnings go, that is all they were. They never gave me a ticket. In fact, the warnings all were based on the harrassment on my 17 year old son The first time the front plate came up, I looked into it and discovered that they were trying to enforce a law by interpreting the law to help back up the harrassment.<BR>Please do not put words in my mouth, or  add statements that I never made.<P>"to adhere to the spirit of the law, which you fought against by attempting to utilize the letter of the law in your defense."<P>And if I am right I am still supposed to just do what I am told? Maybe you, but not me. Sorry. <BR>I understand that some people may have a hard time understanding why this got to where it is, and that we MUST have done something and got a ticket (that didn't get thrown out) which this is all based off of. That is not the case here at all. The DMV have issued rules and suspended my registrations and my license without ever issuing me a ticket or even a written warning. When I called the DMV the other day, I asked this Ann lady what the suspension of my license was based off of. She said I should have gotten a ticket or something a while back that I obviously never followed thru from for this action to be now going into effect. I said no, I was never given a ticket or a written warning or ANYTHING. I asked her if she could go into her computer and look up and see if maybe they sent one that I may never have received. She looked for over 15 minutes and found nothing. She said that usually when a license is suspended, the suspension will reference a number associated with it to show what notice, ticket or written whatever that it would be referencing to. She said she couldn't find anything to refer to in this case. I asked what she thought of that, and that is when we got into having the Chief send a written statement and all. <BR>When the lawyer heard this, I am sure you can guess how strongly he felt how good a case I had.<P>"However, now, instead of:<BR>A - going ahead and mounting the plates on the fronts of your cars,"<P>The plates were mounted on the "front" of our cars. The law does not say where exactly and if the cops or the DMV had a problem with me and where I had them, they had plenty of oportunities to pull me over, give me a ticket, send me a written warning, etc. They didn't, and so they do not have a legal leg to stand on.<P>"B - being slightly disgruntled at the spirit of the law and"<P>The spirit of the law is no more than a interpretation. That is why they hearings or trials or whatever. A hearing would have made sense, to at least try and decide what is the true meaning of the law. At the end of the hearing, if I had lost, at least i would have had my day in court. But I was found guilty without even being a ticket or a trial or hearing or anything. That is a gross misuse of the law, and that my friends is illegal. The DMV decided without a hearing or a trial instead (gee I wonder why?) to make an illegal ruling without any prior hearing or a summons or even so much as a ticket first to base it off from.<P>"C - moving on with your life, "<P>I was, until this latest bull from the DMV where they have illegally suspended my registrations and license. I had even had a conversation with this Plainfield officer Roberts dude on the phone about 2 weeks ago, where he was looking into the plate bracket issue. I think now he was trying to fish for into on if I had the bracket and the plate on yet. Roberts had gotten some part numbers on some brackets from a local Pontiac dealer (the same ones I had told him I had allready talked to), but the bracket numbers he gave me were for a 2M4 model and a coupe model. During this conversation, I told him I had a possibilty of one coming  from Bob Parker at Kick Hill Farms. If he had followed this up before calling Plunket at the DMV and making what turned out to be false statements (remember that he and his Plainfield police dept had allready thrown out the one and only ticket they had issued on this against my son), he would have known that it had arrived and I had it finally on the car. I wonder if he has ever tried any basic investigative work. DUH! I gave him an education on the variety of different Fiero front bumpers earlier, so he would be looking into the correct bracket. He still screwed that all up, not to mention NOT following up on looking into my plate situation and if I did get the bracket from Kick Hill. Double DUH!<P>"you now have <BR>A - the plates mounted on the fronts of your cars,"<P>Thanks again to Bob Parker at Kick Hill for finally finding good used ones for us.<P>"B - scads of legal documentation to fill out,"<P>Wrong. I have no documents to fill out as of yet. If I have to, it will be thru a lawyer and they get to fill that stuff out   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>"C - extra money you are required to pay in order to get the paperwork straightened out,"<P>Not yet. Best case is the paperwork the Chief filled out last night and sent in this morning will hopefully give them an out and they will take it and make it go away.<P>"D - possible points against not only your driving record,"<P>No points lost. That would only have happened if they had actually given me  a ticket. Remember that they never pulled me over. They never gave me a ticket. That is why this is sooo illegal! <P>"but that of your kid(s) who happened to follow your advice,"<P>Again, my son made his own decision. And even after that I stood behind him and fought for him and won to get it thrown out. Why would the police throw it out unless they knew there position was weak?<P>"E - you have the entire local law enforcement community 'gunning' for you, AND your kid(s), AND probably your spouse, just waiting for any of you to make *any* infraction whatsoever so they can cite them or you for something that they can surely enforce."<P>They are not that stupid. Remember that only one Plainfield officer started all this. If the department were try that kind of crap now, they would be just digging a bigger hole. <BR>As bizaare as it sounds, my dad and I know the police, and they know us so we are feeling pretty safe that they won't try that kind of sh_t. . My family has lived in Plainfield for over 40 years. One rookie police officer named Roberts tried some crap a few months ago and that has opened up a can of worms. Now the local police Chief is obviuously scrambling to try and make it all go away. They wouldn't dare try  somethging like that now. It would look really bad on them with all this going on. BUT, if they do, my lawyer and I are ready for that kind of crap if they want to try it.<P>OK, so where is all this right now?<BR>We are still waiting to see what the next move the DMV is going to make. Now that they should have the paperwork from the Chief, are they going to send us a reinstatement letter and that is the end of it? Or are they going to try and make it go on and on and on and try and charge me reinstatement fee's illegally. <BR>If they try that crap, the lawyer said they are ready to take them to court.<P>I will keep you all posted, so<BR>stay tuned.<P>Steve<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero5 (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000029||ChopTop||10-18-2001||07:59 PM||||Write a letter to your Secretary of State.  List the sequence of events by a point by point basis.  Include dates, time, names, and divisions if known. Keep it business like and non-hostile.  Include a copy of the SOS document you received.  Ask for a explanation of why you received misinformation.  Also, ask for the SOS interpretation of the front license plate law.  Put a timeframe for a response.  Your SOS should forward your letter to the appropriate department for a reply. Revise the letter and send it to your district representative along with informing them you are awaiting a response from the SOS.  If you do not receive a reply from the SOS within a resonable amount of time, send a copy of the letter to your representative again asking for their assistance in receiving a response.  If your state is like mine all citizens letters MUST be replied too. Keep a copy of all letters sent, along with a log of date sent.  Always keep orginals, make copies of everything for your lawyer.  Get a copy of the state law and study it.  Good Luck.||||reg||1
Z||000030||LZeitgeist||10-18-2001||07:59 PM||||Any way you want to slice it, if you had put the plate on the car where it was designed to go, none of this would have happened. <P>You brought this on yourself. That does not make us "sheep" - it shows that we have the common sense to choose battles that we have a better chance of winning. You caved in under the pressure put upon you by the police department and the DMV. You lost.<P>"Question authority" all you like. But if you try and piss in the wrong bowl of Cheerios, it only makes *your* life harder, not theirs. I guarantee that *they* don't give a damn whether or not you are able to drive or not.   <P>I give up, hardhead - I've said my piece. ||||reg||1
