Z||000034||Fiero5||10-18-2001||08:51 PM||||LZeitgeist, it looks to me by your continued negative responses here that you have either missed the point or haven't taken the time to actually read the whole story.<BR>"Any way you want to slice it, if you had put the plate on the car where it was designed to go, none of this would have happened."<BR>Gee, Ya think? Now why didn't I think of that?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <BR>Did you actually read any of this dude? I have answered and explained off this type of comment allready many times, so to see the same thing again is getting really old.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <BR>If I am wrong, well I am sorry.<P>Old Lar, the argument the DMV is bringing up is whether the OEM bracket part is still available from the original manufacturer who in this case is GM. So this page out of the Fiero Store is a moot point. If however you are just showing me this for my own information, I paid a lot less for the one from Bob Parker than the one here thru the Fiero store LOL<P>Is it still available thru them though? Now that I think about it,  I had checked with them awhile back and they were out of stock,  not availabale or something. At least at the time I called anyway.<P>Chop Top: Thanks. That is a great idea. This was one of the main reasons I keep posting this besides doing it for those people who just want hear the latest updates . IIt is for the possible chance I may get ideas or suggestions like this. This is a great idea and very helpfull information. I like it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Steve||||reg||1
Z||000035||Tigger||10-18-2001||09:02 PM||||What?  Does that mean my idea of stapling the licence plate to your forehead wasn't a good idea?<P>Just trying to lighten things up.  Hope things go alright for you.||||reg||1
Z||000036||mbramble||10-18-2001||09:30 PM||||Well, I have read it all since the very beginning thread that your father started and I still haven't figured out what the point of it all is.  The idea that the brackets are no longer available from GM is what appears to be moot.  There are lots of items that are no longer available from GM.  It doesn't stop us from getting them where ever we can find them.  But, that wasn't your reasoning for not putting the plates on the car.  Your father posted -- "We do not want to put our plates on the aero nose for three reasons. 1) it makes the Fiero look ugly 2) it causes the flow of air to be obstructed going thru the aero opening 3) it has been said to cause engine heating problems and so forth to the air obstruction."  And then went on to request testimonials that would support those points.  I don't think very many have been provided.  Then he went on to tell about you driving back and forth in front of the cops in order to try and get them to ticket you.  You wanted to test it all in court and maybe you will now get your chance.  So, why complain about what the cops or DMV or anyone else is doing and just take it all to court as youy have wanted to do all along. <P>So, what really is the point here??  <P>1st thread where this is discussed: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009414.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009414.html</A> <P>There is one post by Fiero5 in this post where he indictates that he's not gonna put the plate on the front of his car and that he has "fought the law and I won".  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010624.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010624.html</A> <P>That should give anyone who is interested the full story....<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000037||Fiero5||10-19-2001||09:16 AM||||Tigger, your idea was pretty funny, but sounded very painfull.  LOL<BR>Maybe I could use tape instead?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>mbramble, anyone (like LZeitgeist) who either doesn't understand this thread or just doesn't care has a few choices: <BR>1) Ask questions (I am assuming that in your case mbramble) <BR>2) Hit the back button on their browser.<P>I come accross many threads where once I start reading it, I realize that I either don't understand the subject and/or I just don 't care or whatever. Do I post some silly statement like, "Gee, you broke yer finger while changing the spark plugs? And now yer all upset about it? Well, here is my brilliant opinion on it. You know, you could have avoided the whole thing by just not changing the dang spark plugs". <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <BR>No, I just hit my back button instead. <BR>Simple.<P>"In the begining", we did not have access to a plate bracket when we obtained a Fiero that had the aero nose and, get this, didn't have a front bracket. It was owned by, get this, someone else who lives in NH who had never had a plate on it for all the years they owned it. No biggie we thought, we will just get one. In the process of looking for one, we discovered they were discontinued by GM and that some people had experienced trouble with overheating and other problems apparently due to the blockage in the nose by the front plate. I know that some dissagree with this, but it is our cars (not theirs) we have to maintain<BR>We decided that we didn't want to take the risk, and chose an alternative location in the front of the car. Then this local police officer Roberts decides to make a name for himself, and chose my 17 yr old son in "MY" Fiero to do it. You can read in the other threads about all the times myself and marian drove by this moron and many other police and never once got stopped or warned or anything. This then caused us to look into the front plate law. Knowledge is power folks. We discovered in doing so that the law did not specifically say the plate HAD to be in the front bumper. Soooo, we said ya know what, since the law doesn't say we have to put it there, why are we falling all over ourselves and possibly taking a chance on causing engine/radiator trouble?<BR>Then the DMV thing heated up. My son decides he would like to have it in the nose to just make his problem go away. No problem, we all, stood behind his decision and helped do that. So now that is taken care of, and etc. etc.<P>The rest is all here on this thread.<P>The bottom line here people is that both the Plainfield Police Officer Roberts and Officer Plunket at the DMV have done things that violate anb break the very rules they are supposed to follow. They didn't follow procedure, they didn't issue written warnings to me, give me a ticket or anything.<BR>The "law" says that they are in the wrong. If however the letter from the Chief makes it all go away, then that should be the end of it. If it doesn't, we move to the next level.<BR>The rebel forces attack the Evil DMV Empire and try to take out the two Stormtroopers named Roberts and Plunket  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>John Williams score is playing in the background now while this episodes credits scroll off into space.....<P>Steve<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000038||mbramble||10-19-2001||12:04 PM||||I guess it kind of depends on what is is... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The law your father quoted said plates are to be mounted on the factory provided mounts -- that's a paraphrase.  If there are no factory provided mounts then another section kicks in which is what appears to be the 'ambiguous' part.  <P>Here's where the 'what is is' part comes in -- did the factory provide a mounting point for the front of the car??  In my view, the answer is yes they did.  Your father says "<I>if we agree that on the Indy nose/GT (aero) the original design did not take into effect the creation of a plate mount, this would then have the aero nose style Fieros fall under (c).</I>" (para c being the part that kicks in if there is no factory mount).  It would appear that this is the central point of the argument.  I do not agree with that statement.  Looking at the RPO codes for my aero nosed 85 GT, there is a code for a front mounting plate (according to the Fiero Spotters Guide).  Have I have seen such a thing??  No I haven't.  (of course I never saw the original sail panels, instrument panel, seats, etc. either) Does that mean the factory didn't provide one?  No, it doesn't.  It was either removed, or possibly never mounted by the dealer or original owner but the factory had them available.  They made a provision for mounting a plate on the front of the car and mounts were available to accomplish it.<P>The way I see it, it doesn't really matter whether a particular car was ordered with a front plate mount on it or not.  A mounting point was available from the factory.  I would suspect that the "no factory mounting point" has more to do with old or import or whatever cars that never had a mounting point developed for them by the factory.  In that case that secondary rule kicks in.<P>I don't know if the front plate mount was simply an option, if it was standard with all cars, if it was standard in states that require a front plate all cars -- or what.  I don't have a clue and I'm pretty sure it doesn't matter.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000039||LZeitgeist||10-19-2001||01:17 PM||||I read all your whinings about this situation, and I understand the sequence of events perfectly. There was a simple solution and you chose not to take it. Your current problems have stemmed from there and *only* there. <P>It is obvious that, if anyone refuses to share your pain or take pity on you, you believe they are wrong or stupid. I am far from stupid, and just because you believe someone else to be wrong doesn't make them so. <P>I won't waste any more of my time on self-made victims.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000040||Red2m4||10-19-2001||01:33 PM||||you said:<P>"Then this local police officer Roberts decides to make a name for himself, "<P>I really doubt that he's making a 'name' for himself, I doubt he's getting promoted becuase he caught you with out a plate.  <P>I tend to think that you have a lot of time on your hands, as you are able to spend all this time in court, not to mention the fact that your posts are the longest I have ever seen.  For the time and effort you put into this, you could do a V8 swap !<P>On the other hand, I am kind of curious how it all turns out.  Best of luck.<P>||||reg||1
